# Humanizer writing (user preference — strict for coach)

When writing **for the user** (audits, lessons, landing, onboarding, quiz labels, Notion drafts):

1. Read `~/.agents/skills/humanizer-main/humanizer-main/SKILL.md` (or `@humanizer-main`)
2. Use **simple Russian**, short sentences, no corporate AI words
3. No em dashes, no bold spam, no "pivotal/vibrant/showcase"
4. Explain terms on first use (MCP, hook, skill) in plain words
5. **Prompt coach lessons** — run humanizer pass before save/publish; trim filler; one idea per paragraph

Skip for: code, commit messages, JSON keys, English API docs.

User wants learning materials to feel **human and easy**, not like a chatbot report.
